{"Possible duplicate method definitions in optimized_image.rb - both old downsize method and new downsize(from, to, dimensions, opts={}) may exist": 0.8528713583946228, "Hardcoded max size as 10 * 1024 in JS file instead of using Discourse.SiteSettings, inconsistent with server-side settings": 0.9711418747901917, "In-place tempfile overwrite using OptimizedImage.downsize(tempfile.path, tempfile.path, ...) is fragile and can cause partial writes or file descriptor issues": 0.811564028263092, "Using tempfile.size instead of File.size(tempfile.path) to check file size after downsizing may not reflect the actual on-disk size": 0.9017407298088074, "Repeated downsizing loop with 80% reduction has no check for whether the operation actually changed file size or succeeded": 0.8248409628868103, "No abort mechanism if downsizing fails in the retry loop": 0.7841756343841553, "optimize method signature changed from separate width/height args to single dimensions string without ensuring all call sites are updated": 0.6499286890029907, "GIF detection using filename extension (from =~ /\\.GIF$/i) only checks extension, not whether GIF is actually animated, and could be spoofed": 0.03357508406043053, "Errors during conversion are swallowed with rescue and only logged instead of surfacing appropriate error to the user": 0.468873530626297, "Automatic downsizing runs imagemagick and imageoptim synchronously on web server, which could be expensive with concurrent uploads": 0.3931324779987335, "Missing tests for: upload larger than max size gets downsized, non-image large uploads rejected, failed downsizing returns error, client-side validation uses configured max size": 0.7875869870185852}